  "lessons": "# SCORING LESSONS\n\n- **Indigenous & local community coverage**: Strongly favored across news, wellness, and cultural topics\u2014particularly celebrations, governance, and reconciliation. Local BC/Cariboo stories rank consistently high.\n\n- **Environmental & climate action**: Liked when framed as solutions, protection, or scientific discovery (wildfire response, species preservation, sustainable farming). Less favored when emphasizing disaster or crisis alone.\n\n- **AI skepticism & critical analysis**: Accepts nuanced AI coverage\u2014concerns about speed/deployment, job impact, trust issues, efficiency problems. Dislikes promotional AI product announcements and venture capitalist narratives.\n\n- **Accessible tech how-tos & privacy tips**: Strong preference for practical, user-empowering guides (location tracking, security, free features, cross-device solutions). Rejects product reviews framed as lifestyle aspirations.\n\n- **Journalism & press freedom**: Valued as standalone merit. Dislikes sensationalism, celebrity crime, and human-interest tragedy angles (plane crashes, violent incidents, deaths).\n\n- **Science & nature curiosity**: Favors discovery, behavior, unusual phenomena (sturgeon records, lemur sounds, T-rex growth, brain changes). Rejects wellness pseudoscience and symptom-focused medical advice.\n\n- **Political & social opinion pieces**: Mixed\u2014accepts critical accountability (press freedom, First Nations advocacy). Rejects election coverage, partisan commentary, and culture-war framing.\n\n- **Consumer/lifestyle exclusion zone**: Rejects gear reviews, shopping features, entertainment rankings, fitness optimization, and \"try this trend\" wellness content\u2014even when technically sound.\n\n- **Geopolitical & conflict reporting**: Consistently disliked regardless of source, especially military/violence focus and ceasefire updates.",
